WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:16.858
Baloo grinned proudly as Rann flew off.

2
00:00:16.859 --> 00:00:20.186
"Mowgli remembered the hawk's language!

3
00:00:20.187 --> 00:00:23.706
And he found a way to send us a message."

4
00:00:23.707 --> 00:00:26.273
"See?" Bagheera said.

5
00:00:26.274 --> 00:00:28.967
"I told you that he's very smart.

6
00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:32.484
But we'd better get to Monkey City right away."

7
00:00:32.485 --> 00:00:39.743
Everyone knew where Monkey City was, but few jungle animals went there.

8
00:00:39.744 --> 00:00:44.484
It was an old deserted city, buried in the jungle.

9
00:00:44.485 --> 00:00:50.670
Only the monkeys liked to use places once used by people.

10
00:00:50.671 --> 00:00:57.049
"It is half a night's journey—at full speed," Bagheera said, glancing at the old bear.

11
00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:01.248
"I'll go as fast as I can," Baloo promised.

12
00:01:01.249 --> 00:01:04.104
"We can't wait for you," Bagheera said.

13
00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:08.719
"Kaa and I will rush ahead. You can follow as best you can."

14
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.356
"I have no feet," Kaa said.

15
00:01:12.357 --> 00:01:17.958
"But I'm very fast. Let's go."

16
00:01:17.959 --> 00:01:25.078
Baloo hurried after Kaa and Bagheera, but soon he stopped, panting.

17
00:01:25.079 --> 00:01:33.059
Bagheera kept running, while Kaa seemed to pour himself along the ground.

18
00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:43.158
The snake found the quickest route through the jungle with his steady eyes and followed it.

19
00:01:43.159 --> 00:01:46.137
Mowgli looked around Monkey City.

20
00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:48.345
It was in ruins now.

21
00:01:48.346 --> 00:01:52.005
But some king had built it long ago.

22
00:01:52.006 --> 00:01:58.496
Trees grew in and out of marble walls, and wild vines hung from windows.

23
00:01:58.497 --> 00:02:02.373
There was a palace with no roof at the top of the hill.

24
00:02:02.374 --> 00:02:06.598
Below the palace were rows of houses and empty pits.

25
00:02:06.599 --> 00:02:12.210
Shattered domes from temples lay on the ground.

26
00:02:12.211 --> 00:02:15.412
The monkeys called this place Monkey City.

27
00:02:15.413 --> 00:02:20.160
Yet they had no idea how to use the people's buildings.

28
00:02:20.161 --> 00:02:25.243
They sat inside the marble rooms and scratched for fleas.

29
00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:30.794
They raced along the terrace, shaking orange trees, just to watch the fruit fall.

30
00:02:30.795 --> 00:02:34.685
They drank and fought at the water tanks.

31
00:02:34.686 --> 00:02:38.870
Every once in a while, the monkeys got tired of the city.

32
00:02:38.871 --> 00:02:44.001
Then they went back to the treetops.

33
00:02:44.002 --> 00:02:47.033
The monkeys reached the city late in the day.

34
00:02:47.034 --> 00:02:54.399
Instead of going to sleep after the long journey, the monkeys joined hands and danced.

35
00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:58.971
One monkey even made a long speech.

36
00:02:58.972 --> 00:03:04.903
"This man cub is going to change monkey history!" he announced.

37
00:03:04.904 --> 00:03:12.090
"This boy will show us how to weave sticks together. We can create shelters."

38
00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:17.854
With a sigh, Mowgli began to weave some sticks together.

39
00:03:17.855 --> 00:03:22.988
A few monkeys tried to do just what he was doing.

40
00:03:22.989 --> 00:03:26.808
But one by one, they got bored and jumped up.

41
00:03:26.809 --> 00:03:29.787
Some started pulling friends' tails.

42
00:03:29.788 --> 00:03:32.817
Others jumped around, singing.

43
00:03:32.818 --> 00:03:38.889
Finally Mowgli gave up and put down the sticks. "I'm hungry!"

44
00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:42.835
Twenty monkeys jumped up to bring him nuts.

45
00:03:42.836 --> 00:03:48.179
They started fighting on the way—and forgot all about the food.

46
00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:51.074
"Baloo was right," Mowgli thought.

47
00:03:51.075 --> 00:03:54.541
"Monkeys have no laws and no leader.

48
00:03:54.542 --> 00:03:59.736
All they do is steal and sing. I'm going home!"

49
00:03:59.737 --> 00:04:05.076
Mowgli jumped to his feet and headed toward the gate.

50
00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:08.372
But the monkeys quickly pulled him back.

51
00:04:08.373 --> 00:04:11.255
"Oh no! You're staying with us!"

52
00:04:11.256 --> 00:04:14.643
"Why do you want to leave?" a monkey said.

53
00:04:14.644 --> 00:04:17.283
"We're the most wonderful creatures in the jungle.

54
00:04:17.284 --> 00:04:21.915
We'll tell you all about how great we are!"

55
00:04:21.916 --> 00:04:27.183
All the monkeys were gathering on the terrace to listen to the silly stories.

56
00:04:27.184 --> 00:04:33.091
Mowgli couldn't help laughing.

57
00:04:33.092 --> 00:04:36.673
"I wonder if they ever sleep," he thought.

58
00:04:36.674 --> 00:04:40.890
He looked up to see a cloud sliding toward the moon.

59
00:04:40.891 --> 00:04:44.592
Soon it would be completely dark.

60
00:04:44.593 --> 00:04:49.677
He'd try again to escape then.
